We need to write a Python function is_leap_year(year) returning True if a year is leap year according to Gregorian rules. Must pass given test cases: 2000 True, 1900 False, 2024 True. Provide function implementing rules: divisible by 4 except centuries not divisible by 400. So code:

def is_leap_year(year):
    return (year % 4 == 0 and (year % 100 != 0 or year % 400 == 0))

Make sure to include the assertions. Provide answer.
